# Machine-specific paths and credentials for this repo. Copy to `.env` and edit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is GITIGNORED, and must stay that way: this repo is PUBLIC, and these are
# absolute paths and credentials on your machine. Same name and format as the player
# repo's `.env`, so one block of variables can serve both (a symlink works).
#
# Format is `VAR=value` (no `export`, no quotes needed), which is both make-includable
# (the Makefile `-include`s this file) and shell-sourceable:
#
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#
# Every value below is an EXAMPLE. Nothing here is a real path on anyone's machine -- fill in
# your own.

# Where the ORIGINAL track recordings live -- the `NNN-Artist - Title.ext` files that
# `streamalign track-mix` and the origNNN spans in `streamalign hints` correlate against
# the mix. The repo's `sources` symlink points at an external media volume that is often
# not mounted; point this at a copy that is always there.
#
# This is also where the harvester reads its Mystery Track queries from: a clip named
# `Mystery Track <N>.<wav|mp3|flac|m4a>` puts mystery N into the search. No clip, no search --
# see PROCESS.md, "Adding a new Mystery Track clip".
NETRADIO_SOURCES_DIR=/path/to/your/sources

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube cookies (OPTIONAL -- and OFF by default, deliberately)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube answers anonymous downloads with "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot." That error
# carries no 403 and no 429, so waiting does not clear it: only a signed-in session does. The
# harvester HALTS on it rather than grinding through the queue failing identically on every item.
#
# The cookie IS a credential -- it is your logged-in YouTube session. That is why the harvester
# never goes looking for one on its own, why these are unset by default, and why they live here
# in `.env` (gitignored) and never in the repo.
#
# Set ONE of the two. A cookie FILE wins over a browser if both are set.
#
# 1. A cookies.txt file (Netscape format). PREFERRED on macOS -- it is just a file, so it needs
#    no Keychain, and it will not prompt you. See PROCESS.md, "Feeding the harvester a cookie".
#NETRADIO_YTDLP_COOKIES=/path/to/youtube-cookies.txt
#
# 2. Read them straight out of a browser profile: brave|chrome|chromium|edge|firefox|opera|safari
#    (anything yt-dlp accepts, including a named profile such as `chrome:Profile 2`).
#
#    WARNING, macOS: `chrome` (and any Chromium-based browser) stores its cookies ENCRYPTED and
#    decrypts them through the login Keychain, so every single invocation raises a
#    "security wants to use your ... Chrome Safe Storage" password prompt. A harvester that
#    restarts will prompt you again, and again. `firefox` does NOT have this problem -- it keeps
#    cookies in a plain `cookies.sqlite` -- so prefer firefox, or option 1 above.
#NETRADIO_YTDLP_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=firefox

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live canary (OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `selftest.py`'s LIVE check proves the whole streaming pipeline still works, end to end: it finds
# a stream of a track we have already SOLVED, fetches it, and demands it score as a true match
# against our own copy of that record.
#
# It searches YouTube for the subject's name and takes the first hit -- and for the current subject
# (track 3, Jamie Myerson - Sky Blue) that hit is NOT the record: it scores 0.0867 against our own
# copy, so the guard refuses it. Correct -- a canary that cries wolf is worse than no canary -- but
# it leaves the live check permanently "not checked".
#
# Point it at a stream you know IS the record to break the deadlock. It is still validated against
# our own copy exactly like a searched one: a hand-picked URL is a HINT, never an override.
#NETRADIO_CANARY_URL=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...

# --- Commercial music-ID APIs (scripts/identify_by_api.py) --------------------------------
# Ask ACRCloud/AudD to name a mystery clip against their ~150-160M-track catalogues (which the
# local chroma pool can't reach). NOTE: measured to be defeated by the 1998 ISDN/EQ damage the
# same way AcoustID is -- see Archive/LESSON_acoustid_stream.md. A service is used only if its
# keys are set. Real keys go in .env (gitignored), never here.
#AUDD_API_TOKEN=            # audd.io -- 300 free requests, no card
#ACRCLOUD_HOST=            # identify-<region>.acrcloud.com  (from your ACRCloud project)
#ACRCLOUD_ACCESS_KEY=
#ACRCLOUD_ACCESS_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The cache policy (scripts/cache_budget.py; the same block as the player repo's .env.example)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every cache in both repos registers with cache_budget.py and runs under ONE set of variables.
# A value is set only to depart from the default. `make env-check` reports a name set in .env
# that nothing reads, and a name the code reads that this file does not list.
#
# The floor: the volume holding a cache never passes this percent full, whatever any cap says.
# Nothing is added to any cache while it is; the eviction run evicts across caches by rank until
# it is not. Measured as used/(used+free).
#NETRADIO_DISK_MAX_PCT=82
# The directory every cache's directory defaults under (`<root>/<name>`); the eviction lock and
# the event log live here too. A machine without it runs the policy DARK (nothing is evicted, no
# write is admitted). Both repos read the same value.
#NETRADIO_CACHE_ROOT=/path/to/cache
# How long the event log (events.jsonl under the root) keeps a record. Default 30.
#NETRADIO_CACHE_EVENTS_DAYS=30
#
# Per cache, <NAME> one of STREAMALIGN, LISTENING, HARVEST, KEEP, THUMBS, CLIPS, STREAM_MP3,
# STREAM_MASTER, SOURCES_FLAC, STREAM_TRACKS, CANDIDATES, CHROMA (this repo writes STREAMALIGN,
# CHROMA, CANDIDATES and STREAM_TRACKS; the rest are the player's, listed so one block serves both):
#   NETRADIO_<NAME>_CACHE_GB            the cap in GB (decimal allowed: 0.25 is 250 MB), or none
#   NETRADIO_<NAME>_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB   whole MB no planned-size writer may use (default 0)
#   NETRADIO_<NAME>_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS  evict entries older than this whatever the size, or none
#   NETRADIO_<NAME>_CACHE_DIR           the one directory the cache owns
# Defaults: cap 4 GB except thumbs/clips/candidates 0.25 and stream_mp3/stream_tracks 2; age none
# except streamalign/chroma/stream_tracks 14 and candidates 30; headroom 0 except harvest 500.
#NETRADIO_STREAMALIGN_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_STREAMALIGN_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_STREAMALIGN_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=14
#NETRADIO_STREAMALIGN_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/streamalign
#NETRADIO_CHROMA_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_CHROMA_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_CHROMA_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=14
#NETRADIO_CHROMA_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/chroma
#NETRADIO_CANDIDATES_CACHE_GB=0.25
#NETRADIO_CANDIDATES_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_CANDIDATES_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=30
#NETRADIO_CANDIDATES_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/candidates
#NETRADIO_STREAM_TRACKS_CACHE_GB=2
#NETRADIO_STREAM_TRACKS_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_STREAM_TRACKS_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=14
#NETRADIO_STREAM_TRACKS_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/stream_tracks
#NETRADIO_LISTENING_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_LISTENING_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_LISTENING_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_LISTENING_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/queue/unplayed
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=500
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/queue/harvest
#NETRADIO_KEEP_CACHE_GB=none
#NETRADIO_KEEP_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_KEEP_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_KEEP_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/queue/keep
#NETRADIO_THUMBS_CACHE_GB=0.25
#NETRADIO_THUMBS_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_THUMBS_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_THUMBS_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/queue/thumb_cache
#NETRADIO_CLIPS_CACHE_GB=0.25
#NETRADIO_CLIPS_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_CLIPS_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_CLIPS_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/clips
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MP3_CACHE_GB=2
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MP3_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MP3_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MP3_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/captures/mp3
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MASTER_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MASTER_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MASTER_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_STREAM_MASTER_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/stream_master
#NETRADIO_SOURCES_FLAC_CACHE_GB=4
#NETRADIO_SOURCES_FLAC_CACHE_HEADROOM_MB=0
#NETRADIO_SOURCES_FLAC_CACHE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=none
#NETRADIO_SOURCES_FLAC_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/sources
# The streamalign directory's older name; NETRADIO_STREAMALIGN_CACHE_DIR wins over it.
#NETRADIO_ALIGN_CACHE=/path/to/cache/streamalign

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths, endpoints and knobs the scripts read (rarely set; the defaults are the repo's layout)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The capture files and the labels (defaults: the repo's jaz_links/ and labels/), the player's
# MP3 dir (make_canary.py), the player repo and checkout (the cross-repo sync and streamvideo.py).
#NETRADIO_AUDIO_DIR=/path/to/jaz_links
#NETRADIO_LABELS_DIR=/path/to/labels
#NETRADIO_MP3_DIR=/path/to/jaz_links/mp3
#NETRADIO_PLAYER_REPO=/path/to/netradio_DNB_player
#NETRADIO_PLAYER_DIR=/path/to/netradio_DNB_player
#NETRADIO_ANALYSIS_REPO=/path/to/netradio_DNB_analysis
# The player's URL and download root (harvest.py, match_queue.py); its listen queue path is set
# by the player's supervisor when it starts the harvester.
#NETRADIO_PLAYER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
#NETRADIO_DOWNLOAD_ROOT=/path/to/netradio-queue
#NETRADIO_LISTEN_QUEUE=
# ffmpeg for make_canary.py (else imageio-ffmpeg, else PATH); the canary's source dir.
#NETRADIO_FFMPEG=/path/to/ffmpeg
#NETRADIO_CANARY_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/canary-sources
# The signature store (sigstore.py): an S3-compatible bucket; dark unless the bucket is set.
#NETRADIO_SIG_BUCKET=
#NETRADIO_SIG_S3_ENDPOINT=
#NETRADIO_SIG_AWS_PROFILE=
#NETRADIO_AWS_CLI=/path/to/aws
# The harvester's knobs: the matcher's tries, the parent's restart ceiling (0 = off), the
# missing-signature re-queue cap, and the in-process fetch switch (0 = no child process).
#NETRADIO_CHROMA_TRIES=12
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_MEM_CEILING_MB=0
#NETRADIO_REQUEUE_MISSING_CAP=
#NETRADIO_HARVEST_CHILD=1
# The split harvester (collector.py / harvester.py): enable switches, the controller and its
# tokens, the watcher's hold freshness.
#NETRADIO_COLLECTOR=off
#NETRADIO_HARVESTER=off
#NETRADIO_CONTROLLER_URL=
#NETRADIO_COLLECTOR_TOKEN=
#NETRADIO_FLEET_TOKEN=
#NETRADIO_WATCH_IDLE_S=900
# The Google Sheet backup (backup_sheet.py) and its webhook.
#NETRADIO_SHEET_ID=
#NETRADIO_SHEET_SKIP_TABS=
#NETRADIO_SHEET_WEBHOOK=
# Set by the sync scripts for themselves, never by hand.
#NETRADIO_QUEUE_SYNC=
#NETRADIO_TRACKLIST_SYNC_REEXEC=
